# .graphifyignore — controls what Graphify ingests into the code graph.
#
# ┌─ MODE: DOCS-INCLUDED (active) ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Code + project prose (README, docs/, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) are ingested for  │
# │ rich doc↔code links. Prose semantic extraction runs on your LOCAL Ollama     │
# │ (OpenAI-compatible) → still $0 and private. Run it like:                     │
# │   $env:OPENAI_BASE_URL="http://<mac-host>:11434/v1"                          │
# │   $env:OPENAI_API_KEY="ollama"   # dummy; keeps a misroute failing closed     │
# │   $env:OPENAI_MODEL="qwen2.5:7b-instruct"                                    │
# │   graphify . --backend openai                                                │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# To switch to CODE-ONLY (zero LLM calls, no key needed): uncomment the CODE-ONLY
# block below. (If the doc count won't change after editing, graphify is reusing a
# cache — rerun with `graphify . --force` or delete graphify-out/ first.)
#
# Syntax = .gitignore. Your repo .gitignore is auto-merged, so node_modules, .next,
# /data/wordnet.json, /graphify-out/, etc. are already excluded — not repeated here.
#
# ⚠ NEVER add a `!negation` line — graphify bug #1274: a single `!` disables ALL
#   directory pruning. Keep this an exclude-only blocklist.

# ===== CODE-ONLY MODE — uncomment this whole block to disable every LLM call =====
# *.md
# *.mdx
# *.txt
# *.rst
# docs/
# =================================================================================

# ----- Excluded in BOTH modes -----

# Images — need a vision model; your Ollama roster has none, so these would fail or
# fall back to a cloud key. Keep out.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.svg
*.ico
public/

# PDFs / office / spreadsheets — none in this repo; avoid surprise extraction.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pptx
*.csv

# Audio / video — Whisper transcription; heavy and not architecture.
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# Bundled datasets & lockfiles — graph noise, not architecture.
data/
*.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Tooling / harness meta — skill docs & reports describe the toolchain, not the app.
# (Drop this line if you WANT the .claude/skills/*.md in the graph.)
.claude/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Infra / config dotfiles with no code grammar — zero architectural value, and the
# likely source of the stray "1 doc". Keep excluded in both modes.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
.gitattributes
.prettierignore
.editorconfig
.npmrc
.nvmrc
.env.example
*.example
.graphifyignore

# ----- Optional: drop tests to keep the graph app-focused (tests are local-parsed
#       code, so this is about NOISE, not LLM cost). Uncomment if cluttered:
# tests/
# **/*.test.ts
# **/*.spec.ts
